Type checking passes, but the new reconciliation logic allows unrelated tool or background saves to revive a restart canceled by management-request revocation. This undermines the authorization boundary the patch intends to enforce.

Review comment:

- [P1] Require fresh management authority for pending restart recovery — <cwd>/upstream/superagent/src/app/settings.ts:198-201
  When an account-settings save commits but revocation cancels its deferred restart, an unrelated save can revive that restart without management authorization. A no-op `save('eval', current.eval, revision, 'tool')` reaches this branch with only a lifetime check; automatic policy-sync saves similarly reach the changed-save branch. I reproduced the canceled restart subsequently firing after an unrelated tool save. Restrict pending-restart reconciliation to fresh management authorization instead of allowing tool or background operations to apply the revoked request's account changes.
